Figure 1: EMERGE Early ALMA survey observations in OMC-3. From left to right and from top to bottom we plot
(a) Herschel, total gas column density, $N\mathrm{(H_{2})}$ (36");
(b) WISE 3.4 $\mu$m emission (6.1");
(c) gas kinetic temperature, $T_{\mathrm{K}}$[HCN/HNC],
(d) N2H+ (1-0), and (e) HNC (1-0) obtained with IRAM-30m observations (30");
(f) 3mm continuum emission (ALMA-12m only), plus
(g) N2H+ (1-0) and (h) HNC (1-0) ALMA+IRAM-30m MACF high-resolution (4.5") maps.
The positions of young protostars (cyan triangles) (Megeath et al., 2012) and OB-stars (white stars) are indicated in all panels. The corresponding beam size and scale bar are indicated in the lower corner of each panel. For reference, panel a includes contours at $N\mathrm{(H_{2})}$ = [15, 50, 100, 150, 200] $\times 10^{21}$ cm-2 and the footprint of our ALMA observations. Reference contours in the N2H+ (panel d) and HNC (panel e) IRAM-30m maps are equally spaced every 2.5 and 1.5 K km s-1, respectively.
Similar plots for all the other regions included in this study can be found in (Hacar et al., 2024).

Figure 6: $N\mathrm{(H_{2})}$ column density estimates in OMC-3 at different resolutions. From left to right and from top to bottom:
(a) and (b) Spitzer 3.6, 4.5, 5.8, and 8.0 $\mu m$ color-composed image (Megeath et al., 2012, Credits: Spitzer/NASA/JPL-Caltech; see also )
(c) Herschel map (Lombardi et al., 2014, 36"; );
(d) ArTeMis map (Schuller et al., 2021, 8"; );
(e) $N_{\mathrm{{tot}}}(\mathrm{H_{2})}$ map (4.5"; this work).
To facilitate their comparison, all column density maps are displayed within the same column density range.

